## 5. Rival comparison

### 5.1 OpenClaw

OpenClaw public positioning:

```text
personal AI assistant
run on your own devices
answers on channels you already use
many messaging channels
Gateway is control plane; assistant is the product
```

Also appears as AWS Marketplace one-click browser automation AMI.

Threat:

```text
OpenClaw owns the simple self-hosted/personal-assistant story.
It has a clean pitch: run assistant on your own devices and use existing channels.
```

Empyralis should not compete as “another OpenClaw.”

Empyralis should differentiate as:

```text
governed workspace AI operator OS
Sage + Studio + Agent Computer
personal and business channel separation
hosted managed gateways
local/self-hosted/cloud runtime placement
business-ready policies, approvals, audit, billing
recipes for operational outcomes
```

### 5.2 Poke

Poke public positioning:

```text
assistant through Apple Messages, WhatsApp, Telegram
familiar texting interface
integrations like Notion, Oura, Gmail
recipes
tasks/reminders/proactive help
```

Threat:

```text
Poke is simple.
People understand texting an assistant.
```

Empyralis should copy the lesson, not the exact product.

Empyralis differentiation:

```text
more powerful runtime
Agent Studio
business operations
hardware/computer access
self-hosted/hosted/local gateways
governance and approval system
customer-facing agents
```

Required lesson:

```text
Recipes must hide complexity.
```

### 5.3 Manus

Manus public positioning:

```text
action engine
execute tasks
automate workflows
create slides/websites/apps/design
browser operator
less structure, more intelligence
```

Threat:

```text
Manus is broad and easy to demo.
```

Empyralis differentiation:

```text
persistent business operator
channel ownership
Agent Studio lifecycle
workspace memory/audit
personal + business lanes
hardware runtime control
policy-bound operations
```

Do not compete with Manus on:

```text
do anything once
```

Compete on:

```text
run real business/customer operations every day, safely
```

### 5.4 Meta Business Agent

Meta's AI business-agent direction is a huge competitive threat in WhatsApp/Messenger/Instagram.

Threat:

```text
Meta owns distribution.
It can give businesses native agents inside WhatsApp, Messenger, and Instagram.
```

Empyralis differentiation:

```text
cross-channel
cross-tool
cross-runtime
customer-owned workflows
Telegram/email/web/Slack/Discord support
hardware/computer execution
custom private business logic
stronger workspace-level governance
```

Do not fight Meta head-on inside Meta-owned channels.

Use Meta channels where possible, but make Empyralis the cross-channel operator above them.

### 5.5 NVIDIA NeMo

NVIDIA NeMo is infrastructure for building, optimizing, monitoring, and governing agents.

Threat:

```text
enterprise infra credibility
agent lifecycle/governance language
```

Empyralis differentiation:

```text
end-user product and workspace OS, not only toolkit/framework
```

Lesson:

```text
Use governance/lifecycle/evaluation concepts, but avoid becoming infra-only.
```

